National Research Council. 2001. *Knowing What Students Know: The Science and Design of Educational Assessment*. Committee on the Foundations of Assessment; editors James W. Pellegrino, Naomi Chudowsky and Robert Glaser. English. [Official front matter](https://www.nationalacademies.org/read/10019/chapter/1); DOI [10.17226/10019](https://doi.org/10.17226/10019).

**Reading:** [chapter 2, The Nature of Assessment and Reasoning from Evidence](https://www.nationalacademies.org/read/10019/chapter/4). Compare its framework with the original schedule tasks and identify the assumptions behind your interpretation.

**Inspection, 1 November 2026:** title, editors and copyright; chapter 2 pp. 37–48, including purposes, uncertainty and the cognition/observation/interpretation account. Later chapter sections and the full book are not claimed audited. The broader chapter assignment remains learner work.

